"enc-snip">The Palayakkarar, known in English as Poligars and in Kannada as Palegars, were military chiefs of south India who held territories called palayams under the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/palazzina-di-caccia-of-stupinigi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/palazzina-di-caccia-of-stupinigi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Palazzina di caccia of Stupinigi</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Palazzina di caccia of Stupinigi is a royal hunting lodge south-west of Turin, designed by Filippo Juvarra for King Victor Amadeus II and begun in 1729.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/palazzo-dei-papi-viterbo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/palazzo-dei-papi-viterbo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Palazzo dei Papi (Viterbo)</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Palazzo dei Papi in Viterbo was built from 1255 to 1266 as a residence for the popes, who often lived in the city in the 13th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/palazzo-dei-priori-perugia"><span class="enc-name">Palazzo dei Priori, Perugia</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Palazzo dei Priori is the town hall of Perugia, begun in 1293 and enlarged into the 15th century, facing the Fontana Maggiore.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/palazzo-dei-priori-volterra"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/palazzo-dei-priori-volterra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Palazzo dei Priori, Volterra</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Palazzo dei Priori is the town hall of Volterra in Tuscany, built from 1208 to 1257 and considered the oldest surviving town hall in Tuscany.</span></a></li></ul>
